From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:15:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep the red channel of color dvars

Dvar_RegisterColor stored the red byte through DvarValue::enabled, a
bool, so any non-zero red became 1. Color dvars registered with red
above zero started at red 1/255: g_fogColorReadOnly dumped as
"0.00392157 0 0 1".

Store it through color[0] like the other three channels.
---
 src/universal/dvar.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/universal/dvar.cpp b/src/universal/dvar.cpp
index 0e0eeb72..0970d531 100644
--- a/src/universal/dvar.cpp
+++ b/src/universal/dvar.cpp
@@ -2291,7 +2291,7 @@ const dvar_s *__cdecl Dvar_RegisterColor(
     else
         v8 = 0.0;
     dvarValue.color[3] = SnapFloatToInt(v8 * 255.0f);
-    dvarValue.enabled = SnapFloatToInt(v17 * 255.0f);
+    dvarValue.color[0] = SnapFloatToInt(v17 * 255.0f);
     dvarValue.color[1] = SnapFloatToInt(v14 * 255.0f);
     dvarValue.color[2] = SnapFloatToInt(v11 * 255.0f);
     return Dvar_RegisterVariant(dvarName, DVAR_TYPE_COLOR, flags, dvarValue, 0, description);
